      `either party to that marriage has an additional spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does either party to that marriage have a spouse additional to the other party?
      `my spouse, the other party and the additional spouse are in one household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, the other party to the marriage and the additional spouse members of the same household?
      `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a pilot scheme made under section 18A apply to you?
      `the standard minimum guarantee for a couple, a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple, a week, in the regulations in force on that day? (The Act states no figure.)
      `the standard minimum guarantee for a single person, a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the (lower) standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple, a week?
      `the additional amount for a severely disabled claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc What additional amount do the regulations include for a severely disabled claimant? (0 if none.)
      `the additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What additional amount do the regulations include where an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment is due? (0 if none.)
      `other additional amounts that apply to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What other additional amounts do the regulations include in your appropriate minimum guarantee? (0 if none.)
      `the regulations fix a substitute for the standard minimum guarantee in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your case, do the regulations under section 2(6) put a prescribed amount in place of the standard minimum guarantee?
      `that substitute amount` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what is that amount? (0 if not.)
      `the savings credit threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the savings credit threshold in the regulations in force on that day?
      `the percentage used for amount A` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations use for amount A (section 3(4))? (60 means 60 per cent.)
      `the percentage used for amount B` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations use for amount B (section 3(4))?
      `the percentage used for the maximum savings credit` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations use for the maximum savings credit (section 3(7))?
      `the regulations fix a higher amount for amount B in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your case, do the regulations under section 3(5) put a prescribed higher amount in place of the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B?
      `that higher amount for amount B` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what is that higher amount? (0 if not.)
      `I have made a claim for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a claim for state pension credit, with the national insurance number and evidence the Administration Act asks for?
      `section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998 restricts my entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998 (a restriction after an error) apply to you?
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `whether I am entitled to state pension credit` IS
    `The Act's answer on whether the claimant is entitled to state pension credit` `my case` `the prescribed figures`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day I reach pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age`
        `my partner` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my partner's sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my partner's date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day my partner reaches pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my partner's birthday reaches pensionable age`
        `my household` MEANS Household WITH
            `married to or civil partners of each other` IS `my partner and I are married or civil partners`
            `members of the same household` IS `my partner and I are members of the same household`
            `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners`
            `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb`
        `my income` MEANS Income WITH
            earnings IS `my weekly earnings`
            `working tax credit` IS `my weekly working tax credit`
            `retirement pension income` IS `my weekly retirement pension income`
            `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS `my weekly annuity income that is not retirement pension income`
            `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS `my weekly prescribed social security benefits`
            `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS `my weekly foreign social security benefits`
            `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my weekly war pensions`
            `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my weekly foreign war pensions`
            `income from capital` IS `my weekly income from capital`
            `income of a prescribed description` IS `my weekly other income of a prescribed kind`
        `my partner's income` MEANS Income WITH
            earnings IS `my partner's weekly earnings`
            `working tax credit` IS `my partner's weekly working tax credit`
            `retirement pension income` IS `my partner's weekly retirement pension income`
            `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS `my partner's weekly annuity income that is not retirement pension income`
            `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS `my partner's weekly prescribed social security benefits`
            `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS `my partner's weekly foreign social security benefits`
            `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my partner's weekly war pensions`
            `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my partner's weekly foreign war pensions`
            `income from capital` IS `my partner's weekly income from capital`
            `income of a prescribed description` IS `my partner's weekly other income of a prescribed kind`
        `my case` MEANS Case WITH
            `day tested` IS `the day I am asking about`
            claimant IS `me`
            `other member of the couple` IS `my partner`
            household IS `my household`
            `in Great Britain` IS `I am in Great Britain`
            `temporarily absent from Great Britain and entitlement continued by regulations` IS `I am away from Great Britain for a while and the regulations keep my entitlement going`
            `income of the claimant` IS `my income`
            `qualifying income of the claimant` IS `my qualifying income`
            `income of the other member` IS `my partner's income`
            `qualifying income of the other member` IS `my partner's qualifying income`
            `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated` IS `the regulations say my partner's income is not counted with mine`
            `severely disabled` IS `I am severely disabled`
            `claimant entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS `I am entitled to an allowance under section 70 or to carer support payment`
            `other member entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS `my partner is entitled to such an allowance or payment`
            `other member entitled to state pension credit` IS `my partner is already entitled to state pension credit`
            `regulations under section 3ZA(1) prescribe the claimant's case` IS `the regulations stop me getting a savings credit as a member of a mixed-age couple`
            `regulations under section 3(8) take the maximum savings credit to be nil` IS `the regulations take my maximum savings credit to be nil`
            `excluded by section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 as amended by section 4(2)` IS `section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 excludes me`
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `prescribed circumstances in which an amount below the prescribed amount is payable` IS FALSE
            `a claim has been made and the Administration Act section 1 conditions are met` IS `I have made a claim for state pension credit`
            `entitlement restricted by section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS `section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998 restricts my entitlement`
            `husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy` IS `I am a husband or wife by a marriage under a law that permits polygamy`
            `either party to the marriage has a spouse additional to the other party` IS `either party to that marriage has an additional spouse`
            `person, other party and additional spouse members of the same household` IS `my spouse, the other party and the additional spouse are in one household`
            `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies` IS `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies to me`
        `the prescribed figures` MEANS Prescribed WITH
            `standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple` IS `the standard minimum guarantee for a couple, a week`
            `standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple` IS `the standard minimum guarantee for a single person, a week`
            `additional amount for a claimant who is severely disabled` IS `the additional amount for a severely disabled claimant`
            `additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS `the additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment`
            `other prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` IS `other additional amounts that apply to me`
            `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` IS IF `the regulations fix a substitute for the standard minimum guarantee in my case` THEN JUST `that substitute amount` ELSE NOTHING
            `savings credit threshold` IS `the savings credit threshold`
            `prescribed percentage for amount A` IS `the percentage used for amount A`
            `prescribed percentage for amount B` IS `the percentage used for amount B`
            `prescribed percentage for the maximum savings credit` IS `the percentage used for the maximum savings credit`
            `prescribed higher amount substituted for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` IS IF `the regulations fix a higher amount for amount B in my case` THEN JUST `that higher amount for amount B` ELSE NOTHING
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read the minimum payable.
            `prescribed amount below which state pension credit is not payable` IS 0

@export Have I reached the qualifying age for state pension credit (s 1(2)(b), (6))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know where you stand? (Use today's date unless you are asking about another day.)
      `my sex` IS A Sex @desc Are you a woman or a man? (Section 1(6) treats them differently.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you reach, or did you reach, pensionable age (the age the Pensions Act 1995 sets for you)?
      `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, a woman born on your date of birth reach pensionable age? (If you are a woman, give the same day as the answer above.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `whether I have reached the qualifying age` IF
    `s 1(6) -- has attained the qualifying age on` `the day I am asking about` `me`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day I reach pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age`

§§ `2 Guarantee credit`

@export How much guarantee credit am I entitled to, a week (s 2)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know where you stand? (Use today's date unless you are asking about another day.)
      `my sex` IS A Sex @desc Are you a woman or a man? (Section 1(6) treats them differently.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you reach, or did you reach, pensionable age (the age the Pensions Act 1995 sets for you)?
      `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, a woman born on your date of birth reach pensionable age? (If you are a woman, give the same day as the answer above.)
      `I am in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Great Britain? (Answer as the regulations treat you: they may count you as in or out.)
      `I am away from Great Britain for a while and the regulations keep my entitlement going` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are away from Great Britain, is it only for a while, and do the regulations keep your entitlement going during the absence?
      `my partner and I are married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you married to, or in a civil partnership with, the person you live with? (No if you live alone or with someone you are not married to.)
      `my partner and I are members of the same household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and that person members of the same household?
      `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not married to or in a civil partnership with that person, do you live together as if you were?
      `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations say that, in your circumstances, you are not to be treated as living together as a couple?
      `my partner's sex` IS A Sex @desc Is your partner a woman or a man? (Answer anything if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your partner's date of birth? (Any date if you have no partner.)
      `the day my partner reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, your partner reach pensionable age? (Any date if you have no partner.)
      `the day a woman born on my partner's birthday reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, a woman born on your partner's date of birth reach pensionable age? (If your partner is a woman, the same day as the answer above.)
      `my partner is already entitled to state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner already entitled to state pension credit?
      `my weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you earn each week?
      `my weekly working tax credit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much working tax credit do you get each week?
      `my weekly retirement pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much retirement pension income do you get each week (state pension, other pensions, annuities from pension schemes, and the other kinds in section 16(1))?
      `my weekly annuity income that is not retirement pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much income from annuity contracts, other than retirement pension income, do you get each week?
      `my weekly prescribed social security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you get each week in social security benefits the regulations list (other than retirement pension income and state pension credit)?
      `my weekly foreign social security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you get each week in foreign social security benefits of a kind the regulations list?
      `my weekly war pensions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension do you get each week?
      `my weekly foreign war pensions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension do you get each week?
      `my weekly income from capital` IS A NUMBER @desc How much income from capital do you have each week (including income the regulations treat your capital as yielding)?
      `my weekly other income of a prescribed kind` IS A NUMBER @desc How much other income of a kind the regulations list do you have each week?
      `my qualifying income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your income counts as qualifying income each week, as the regulations work it out (section 3(6))? (Give 0 if none of it counts.)
      `my partner's weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your partner earn each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly working tax credit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much working tax credit does your partner get each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly retirement pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much retirement pension income does your partner get each week (state pension, other pensions, annuities from pension schemes, and the other kinds in section 16(1))? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly annuity income that is not retirement pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much income from annuity contracts, other than retirement pension income, does your partner get each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly prescribed social security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your partner get each week in social security benefits the regulations list (other than retirement pension income and state pension credit)? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly foreign social security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your partner get each week in foreign social security benefits of a kind the regulations list? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly war pensions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension does your partner get each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly foreign war pensions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension does your partner get each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly income from capital` IS A NUMBER @desc How much income from capital does your partner have each week (including income the regulations treat their capital as yielding)? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly other income of a prescribed kind` IS A NUMBER @desc How much other income of a kind the regulations list does your partner have each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's qualifying income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your partner's income counts as qualifying income each week, as the regulations work it out? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `the regulations say my partner's income is not counted with mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations say that, in your circumstances, your partner's income and capital are not to be counted as yours?
      `I am severely disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you severely disabled, as the regulations treat you?
      `I am entitled to an allowance under section 70 or to carer support payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (carer's allowance), or to carer support payment?
      `my partner is entitled to such an allowance or payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner entitled to such an allowance, or to carer support payment? (No if you have no partner.)
      `the regulations stop me getting a savings credit as a member of a mixed-age couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations under section 3ZA(1) say you are not entitled to a savings credit as a member of a mixed-age couple?
      `the regulations take my maximum savings credit to be nil` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations under section 3(8) say your maximum savings credit is nil?
      `section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 excludes me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 exclude you from state pension credit?
      `I am a husband or wife by a marriage under a law that permits polygamy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy?
      `either party to that marriage has an additional spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does either party to that marriage have a spouse additional to the other party?
      `my spouse, the other party and the additional spouse are in one household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, the other party to the marriage and the additional spouse members of the same household?
      `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a pilot scheme made under section 18A apply to you?
      `the standard minimum guarantee for a couple, a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple, a week, in the regulations in force on that day? (The Act states no figure.)
      `the standard minimum guarantee for a single person, a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the (lower) standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple, a week?
      `the additional amount for a severely disabled claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc What additional amount do the regulations include for a severely disabled claimant? (0 if none.)
      `the additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What additional amount do the regulations include where an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment is due? (0 if none.)
      `other additional amounts that apply to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What other additional amounts do the regulations include in your appropriate minimum guarantee? (0 if none.)
      `the regulations fix a substitute for the standard minimum guarantee in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your case, do the regulations under section 2(6) put a prescribed amount in place of the standard minimum guarantee?
      `that substitute amount` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what is that amount? (0 if not.)
      `the savings credit threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the savings credit threshold in the regulations in force on that day?
      `the percentage used for amount A` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations use for amount A (section 3(4))? (60 means 60 per cent.)
      `the percentage used for amount B` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations use for amount B (section 3(4))?
      `the percentage used for the maximum savings credit` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations use for the maximum savings credit (section 3(7))?
      `the regulations fix a higher amount for amount B in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your case, do the regulations under section 3(5) put a prescribed higher amount in place of the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B?
      `that higher amount for amount B` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what is that higher amount? (0 if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the guarantee credit I am entitled to` IS
    IF `s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` `my case`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`s 2(2) -- the guarantee credit to which the claimant is entitled` `my case` `the prescribed figures`)
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day I reach pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age`
        `my partner` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my partner's sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my partner's date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day my partner reaches pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my partner's birthday reaches pensionable age`
        `my household` MEANS Household WITH
            `married to or civil partners of each other` IS `my partner and I are married or civil partners`
            `members of the same household` IS `my partner and I are members of the same household`
            `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners`
            `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb`
        `my income` MEANS Income WITH
            earnings IS `my weekly earnings`
            `working tax credit` IS `my weekly working tax credit`
            `retirement pension income` IS `my weekly retirement pension income`
            `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS `my weekly annuity income that is not retirement pension income`
            `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS `my weekly prescribed social security benefits`
            `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS `my weekly foreign social security benefits`
            `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my weekly war pensions`
            `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my weekly foreign war pensions`
            `income from capital` IS `my weekly income from capital`
            `income of a prescribed description` IS `my weekly other income of a prescribed kind`
        `my partner's income` MEANS Income WITH
            earnings IS `my partner's weekly earnings`
            `working tax credit` IS `my partner's weekly working tax credit`
            `retirement pension income` IS `my partner's weekly retirement pension income`
            `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS `my partner's weekly annuity income that is not retirement pension income`
            `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS `my partner's weekly prescribed social security benefits`
            `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS `my partner's weekly foreign social security benefits`
            `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my partner's weekly war pensions`
            `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my partner's weekly foreign war pensions`
            `income from capital` IS `my partner's weekly income from capital`
            `income of a prescribed description` IS `my partner's weekly other income of a prescribed kind`
        `my case` MEANS Case WITH
            `day tested` IS `the day I am asking about`
            claimant IS `me`
            `other member of the couple` IS `my partner`
            household IS `my household`
            `in Great Britain` IS `I am in Great Britain`
            `temporarily absent from Great Britain and entitlement continued by regulations` IS `I am away from Great Britain for a while and the regulations keep my entitlement going`
            `income of the claimant` IS `my income`
            `qualifying income of the claimant` IS `my qualifying income`
            `income of the other member` IS `my partner's income`
            `qualifying income of the other member` IS `my partner's qualifying income`
            `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated` IS `the regulations say my partner's income is not counted with mine`
            `severely disabled` IS `I am severely disabled`
            `claimant entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS `I am entitled to an allowance under section 70 or to carer support payment`
            `other member entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS `my partner is entitled to such an allowance or payment`
            `other member entitled to state pension credit` IS `my partner is already entitled to state pension credit`
            `regulations under section 3ZA(1) prescribe the claimant's case` IS `the regulations stop me getting a savings credit as a member of a mixed-age couple`
            `regulations under section 3(8) take the maximum savings credit to be nil` IS `the regulations take my maximum savings credit to be nil`
            `excluded by section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 as amended by section 4(2)` IS `section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 excludes me`
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `prescribed circumstances in which an amount below the prescribed amount is payable` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `a claim has been made and the Administration Act section 1 conditions are met` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `entitlement restricted by section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS FALSE
            `husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy` IS `I am a husband or wife by a marriage under a law that permits polygamy`
            `either party to the marriage has a spouse additional to the other party` IS `either party to that marriage has an additional spouse`
            `person, other party and additional spouse members of the same household` IS `my spouse, the other party and the additional spouse are in one household`
            `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies` IS `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies to me`
        `the prescribed figures` MEANS Prescribed WITH
            `standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple` IS `the standard minimum guarantee for a couple, a week`
            `standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple` IS `the standard minimum guarantee for a single person, a week`
            `additional amount for a claimant who is severely disabled` IS `the additional amount for a severely disabled claimant`
            `additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS `the additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment`
            `other prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` IS `other additional amounts that apply to me`
            `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` IS IF `the regulations fix a substitute for the standard minimum guarantee in my case` THEN JUST `that substitute amount` ELSE NOTHING
            `savings credit threshold` IS `the savings credit threshold`
            `prescribed percentage for amount A` IS `the percentage used for amount A`
            `prescribed percentage for amount B` IS `the percentage used for amount B`
            `prescribed percentage for the maximum savings credit` IS `the percentage used for the maximum savings credit`
            `prescribed higher amount substituted for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` IS IF `the regulations fix a higher amount for amount B in my case` THEN JUST `that higher amount for amount B` ELSE NOTHING
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read the minimum payable.
            `prescribed amount below which state pension credit is not payable` IS 0

§§ `3 Savings credit`

@export How much savings credit am I entitled to, a week (s 3)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know where you stand? (Use today's date unless you are asking about another day.)
      `my sex` IS A Sex @desc Are you a woman or a man? (Section 1(6) treats them differently.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you reach, or did you reach, pensionable age (the age the Pensions Act 1995 sets for you)?
      `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, a woman born on your date of birth reach pensionable age? (If you are a woman, give the same day as the answer above.)
      `I am in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Great Britain? (Answer as the regulations treat you: they may count you as in or out.)
      `I am away from Great Britain for a while and the regulations keep my entitlement going` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are away from Great Britain, is it only for a while, and do the regulations keep your entitlement going during the absence?
      `my partner and I are married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you married to, or in a civil partnership with, the person you live with? (No if you live alone or with someone you are not married to.)
      `my partner and I are members of the same household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and that person members of the same household?
      `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not married to or in a civil partnership with that person, do you live together as if you were?
      `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations say that, in your circumstances, you are not to be treated as living together as a couple?
      `my partner's sex` IS A Sex @desc Is your partner a woman or a man? (Answer anything if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your partner's date of birth? (Any date if you have no partner.)
      `the day my partner reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, your partner reach pensionable age? (Any date if you have no partner.)
      `the day a woman born on my partner's birthday reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, a woman born on your partner's date of birth reach pensionable age? (If your partner is a woman, the same day as the answer above.)
      `my partner is already entitled to state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner already entitled to state pension credit?
      `my weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you earn each week?
      `my weekly working tax credit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much working tax credit do you get each week?
      `my weekly retirement pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much retirement pension income do you get each week (state pension, other pensions, annuities from pension schemes, and the other kinds in section 16(1))?
      `my weekly annuity income that is not retirement pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much income from annuity contracts, other than retirement pension income, do you get each week?
      `my weekly prescribed social security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you get each week in social security benefits the regulations list (other than retirement pension income and state pension credit)?
      `my weekly foreign social security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you get each week in foreign social security benefits of a kind the regulations list?
      `my weekly war pensions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension do you get each week?
      `my weekly foreign war pensions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension do you get each week?
      `my weekly income from capital` IS A NUMBER @desc How much income from capital do you have each week (including income the regulations treat your capital as yielding)?
      `my weekly other income of a prescribed kind` IS A NUMBER @desc How much other income of a kind the regulations list do you have each week?
      `my qualifying income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your income counts as qualifying income each week, as the regulations work it out (section 3(6))? (Give 0 if none of it counts.)
      `my partner's weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your partner earn each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly working tax credit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much working tax credit does your partner get each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly retirement pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much retirement pension income does your partner get each week (state pension, other pensions, annuities from pension schemes, and the other kinds in section 16(1))? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly annuity income that is not retirement pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much income from annuity contracts, other than retirement pension income, does your partner get each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly prescribed social security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your partner get each week in social security benefits the regulations list (other than retirement pension income and state pension credit)? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly foreign social security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your partner get each week in foreign social security benefits of a kind the regulations list? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly war pensions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension does your partner get each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly foreign war pensions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension does your partner get each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly income from capital` IS A NUMBER @desc How much income from capital does your partner have each week (including income the regulations treat their capital as yielding)? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's weekly other income of a prescribed kind` IS A NUMBER @desc How much other income of a kind the regulations list does your partner have each week? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's qualifying income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your partner's income counts as qualifying income each week, as the regulations work it out? (0 if you have no partner.)
      `the regulations say my partner's income is not counted with mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations say that, in your circumstances, your partner's income and capital are not to be counted as yours?
      `I am severely disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you severely disabled, as the regulations treat you?
      `I am entitled to an allowance under section 70 or to carer support payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (carer's allowance), or to carer support payment?
      `my partner is entitled to such an allowance or payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner entitled to such an allowance, or to carer support payment? (No if you have no partner.)
      `the regulations stop me getting a savings credit as a member of a mixed-age couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations under section 3ZA(1) say you are not entitled to a savings credit as a member of a mixed-age couple?
      `the regulations take my maximum savings credit to be nil` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations under section 3(8) say your maximum savings credit is nil?
      `section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 excludes me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 exclude you from state pension credit?
      `I am a husband or wife by a marriage under a law that permits polygamy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy?
      `either party to that marriage has an additional spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does either party to that marriage have a spouse additional to the other party?
      `my spouse, the other party and the additional spouse are in one household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, the other party to the marriage and the additional spouse members of the same household?
      `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a pilot scheme made under section 18A apply to you?
      `the standard minimum guarantee for a couple, a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple, a week, in the regulations in force on that day? (The Act states no figure.)
      `the standard minimum guarantee for a single person, a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the (lower) standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple, a week?
      `the additional amount for a severely disabled claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc What additional amount do the regulations include for a severely disabled claimant? (0 if none.)
      `the additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What additional amount do the regulations include where an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment is due? (0 if none.)
      `other additional amounts that apply to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What other additional amounts do the regulations include in your appropriate minimum guarantee? (0 if none.)
      `the regulations fix a substitute for the standard minimum guarantee in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your case, do the regulations under section 2(6) put a prescribed amount in place of the standard minimum guarantee?
      `that substitute amount` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what is that amount? (0 if not.)
      `the savings credit threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the savings credit threshold in the regulations in force on that day?
      `the percentage used for amount A` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations use for amount A (section 3(4))? (60 means 60 per cent.)
      `the percentage used for amount B` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations use for amount B (section 3(4))?
      `the percentage used for the maximum savings credit` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations use for the maximum savings credit (section 3(7))?
      `the regulations fix a higher amount for amount B in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your case, do the regulations under section 3(5) put a prescribed higher amount in place of the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B?
      `that higher amount for amount B` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what is that higher amount? (0 if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the savings credit I am entitled to` IS
    IF `s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` `my case`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`s 3(3) -- the savings credit to which the claimant is entitled` `my case` `the prescribed figures`)
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day I reach pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age`
        `my partner` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my partner's sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my partner's date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day my partner reaches pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my partner's birthday reaches pensionable age`
        `my household` MEANS Household WITH
            `married to or civil partners of each other` IS `my partner and I are married or civil partners`
            `members of the same household` IS `my partner and I are members of the same household`
            `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners`
            `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb`
        `my income` MEANS Income WITH
            earnings IS `my weekly earnings`
            `working tax credit` IS `my weekly working tax credit`
            `retirement pension income` IS `my weekly retirement pension income`
            `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS `my weekly annuity income that is not retirement pension income`
            `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS `my weekly prescribed social security benefits`
            `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS `my weekly foreign social security benefits`
            `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my weekly war pensions`
            `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my weekly foreign war pensions`
            `income from capital` IS `my weekly income from capital`
            `income of a prescribed description` IS `my weekly other income of a prescribed kind`
        `my partner's income` MEANS Income WITH
            earnings IS `my partner's weekly earnings`
            `working tax credit` IS `my partner's weekly working tax credit`
            `retirement pension income` IS `my partner's weekly retirement pension income`
            `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS `my partner's weekly annuity income that is not retirement pension income`
            `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS `my partner's weekly prescribed social security benefits`
            `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS `my partner's weekly foreign social security benefits`
            `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my partner's weekly war pensions`
            `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS `my partner's weekly foreign war pensions`
            `income from capital` IS `my partner's weekly income from capital`
            `income of a prescribed description` IS `my partner's weekly other income of a prescribed kind`
        `my case` MEANS Case WITH
            `day tested` IS `the day I am asking about`
            claimant IS `me`
            `other member of the couple` IS `my partner`
            household IS `my household`
            `in Great Britain` IS `I am in Great Britain`
            `temporarily absent from Great Britain and entitlement continued by regulations` IS `I am away from Great Britain for a while and the regulations keep my entitlement going`
            `income of the claimant` IS `my income`
            `qualifying income of the claimant` IS `my qualifying income`
            `income of the other member` IS `my partner's income`
            `qualifying income of the other member` IS `my partner's qualifying income`
            `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated` IS `the regulations say my partner's income is not counted with mine`
            `severely disabled` IS `I am severely disabled`
            `claimant entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS `I am entitled to an allowance under section 70 or to carer support payment`
            `other member entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS `my partner is entitled to such an allowance or payment`
            `other member entitled to state pension credit` IS `my partner is already entitled to state pension credit`
            `regulations under section 3ZA(1) prescribe the claimant's case` IS `the regulations stop me getting a savings credit as a member of a mixed-age couple`
            `regulations under section 3(8) take the maximum savings credit to be nil` IS `the regulations take my maximum savings credit to be nil`
            `excluded by section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 as amended by section 4(2)` IS `section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 excludes me`
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `prescribed circumstances in which an amount below the prescribed amount is payable` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `a claim has been made and the Administration Act section 1 conditions are met` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `entitlement restricted by section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS FALSE
            `husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy` IS `I am a husband or wife by a marriage under a law that permits polygamy`
            `either party to the marriage has a spouse additional to the other party` IS `either party to that marriage has an additional spouse`
            `person, other party and additional spouse members of the same household` IS `my spouse, the other party and the additional spouse are in one household`
            `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies` IS `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies to me`
        `the prescribed figures` MEANS Prescribed WITH
            `standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple` IS `the standard minimum guarantee for a couple, a week`
            `standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple` IS `the standard minimum guarantee for a single person, a week`
            `additional amount for a claimant who is severely disabled` IS `the additional amount for a severely disabled claimant`
            `additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS `the additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment`
            `other prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` IS `other additional amounts that apply to me`
            `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` IS IF `the regulations fix a substitute for the standard minimum guarantee in my case` THEN JUST `that substitute amount` ELSE NOTHING
            `savings credit threshold` IS `the savings credit threshold`
            `prescribed percentage for amount A` IS `the percentage used for amount A`
            `prescribed percentage for amount B` IS `the percentage used for amount B`
            `prescribed percentage for the maximum savings credit` IS `the percentage used for the maximum savings credit`
            `prescribed higher amount substituted for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` IS IF `the regulations fix a higher amount for amount B in my case` THEN JUST `that higher amount for amount B` ELSE NOTHING
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read the minimum payable.
            `prescribed amount below which state pension credit is not payable` IS 0

@export Do I meet the age condition for the savings credit (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know where you stand? (Use today's date unless you are asking about another day.)
      `my sex` IS A Sex @desc Are you a woman or a man? (Section 1(6) treats them differently.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you reach, or did you reach, pensionable age (the age the Pensions Act 1995 sets for you)?
      `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, a woman born on your date of birth reach pensionable age? (If you are a woman, give the same day as the answer above.)
      `my partner and I are married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you married to, or in a civil partnership with, the person you live with? (No if you live alone or with someone you are not married to.)
      `my partner and I are members of the same household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and that person members of the same household?
      `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not married to or in a civil partnership with that person, do you live together as if you were?
      `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations say that, in your circumstances, you are not to be treated as living together as a couple?
      `my partner's sex` IS A Sex @desc Is your partner a woman or a man? (Answer anything if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your partner's date of birth? (Any date if you have no partner.)
      `the day my partner reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, your partner reach pensionable age? (Any date if you have no partner.)
      `the day a woman born on my partner's birthday reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, a woman born on your partner's date of birth reach pensionable age? (If your partner is a woman, the same day as the answer above.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `whether I meet the age condition for the savings credit` IF
    `s 3(1) -- the first savings credit condition` `my case`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day I reach pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age`
        `my partner` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my partner's sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my partner's date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day my partner reaches pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my partner's birthday reaches pensionable age`
        `my household` MEANS Household WITH
            `married to or civil partners of each other` IS `my partner and I are married or civil partners`
            `members of the same household` IS `my partner and I are members of the same household`
            `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners`
            `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb`
        -- Placeholder: this question does not read this income.
        `my income` MEANS Income WITH
            earnings IS 0
            `working tax credit` IS 0
            `retirement pension income` IS 0
            `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS 0
            `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS 0
            `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS 0
            `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
            `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
            `income from capital` IS 0
            `income of a prescribed description` IS 0
        -- Placeholder: this question does not read this income.
        `my partner's income` MEANS Income WITH
            earnings IS 0
            `working tax credit` IS 0
            `retirement pension income` IS 0
            `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS 0
            `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS 0
            `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS 0
            `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
            `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
            `income from capital` IS 0
            `income of a prescribed description` IS 0
        `my case` MEANS Case WITH
