§§ `7 Fixing of claimant's retirement provision for assessed income period`

@export Is this kind of income part of my retirement provision (s 7(6))?
GIVEN `this kind of income` IS A `Description of income` @desc Which kind of income is it?
      `the payment was ordered by a court or made in settlement of a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a payment by a former employer on early retirement, was it ordered by a court or made in settlement of a claim?
      `the payment is made under the law of Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under the law of Northern Ireland?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `whether this income is part of my retirement provision` IF
    `s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `this kind of income` `the payment was ordered by a court or made in settlement of a claim` `the payment is made under the law of Northern Ireland`

@export What amount of this income is counted for my assessed income period on a given day (s 7(3) to (5))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know where you stand? (Use today's date unless you are asking about another day.)
      `the amount fixed for this income at the decision` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount of this income was fixed (assessed) when the decision was made, a week?
      `this income is income from capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this income from capital?
      `the decision counted this income as part of mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the decision count this income as part of yours?
      `the regulations stop the amount varying in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations prescribe circumstances in which this amount is not treated as varying in your case?
      `a change of this amount is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations prescribe a date on which this amount is treated as changing?
      `the day that change takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does that change take effect? (Any date if none.)
      `the amount of that change` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much does it change, a week? (A decrease is negative; 0 if none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount of this income counted on the day` IS
    `s 7(3) to (5) -- the amount of the element on` `the day I am asking about` `my income element`
    WHERE
        `my income element` MEANS `Element of retirement provision` WITH
            `assessed amount` IS `the amount fixed for this income at the decision`
            `income from capital` IS `this income is income from capital`
            `included in the claimant's income as determined for the relevant decision` IS `the decision counted this income as part of mine`
            `variations prescribed under section 7(4)` IS
                IF `a change of this amount is prescribed`
                THEN LIST (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS `the day that change takes effect`, `amount of the variation` IS `the amount of that change`)
                ELSE EMPTY
            `prescribed circumstances in which the assessed amount is not deemed to vary` IS `the regulations stop the amount varying in my case`

§§ `8 Fresh determinations increasing claimant's entitlement`

@export Can fresh determinations of my retirement provision be made during my period (s 8(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the new decision is a decision under section 10 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new decision a decision under section 10 of the Social Security Act 1998?
      `the increase is partly or wholly the result of the fresh determinations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the increase in your state pension credit wholly or partly the result of the fresh determinations of your retirement provision?
      `my state pension credit before the new decision` IS A NUMBER @desc How much state pension credit were you entitled to before the new decision, a week?
      `my state pension credit under the new decision` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are you entitled to under the new decision, a week?
      `my state pension credit under the new decision apart from the fresh determinations` IS A NUMBER @desc How much would you have been entitled to under the new decision without the fresh determinations, a week?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `whether fresh determinations of my retirement provision may be made` IF
    `s 8(1), (2) -- fresh determinations may be made` `the new decision is a decision under section 10 of the Social Security Act 1998` `the increase is partly or wholly the result of the fresh determinations` `my state pension credit before the new decision` `my state pension credit under the new decision` `my state pension credit under the new decision apart from the fresh determinations`

@export Which determination of my retirement provision governs on a given day (s 8(3))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know where you stand? (Use today's date unless you are asking about another day.)
      `the day the new decision takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the new decision take effect?
GIVETH A `Which determination governs`
DECIDE `which determination governs on the day` IS
    `s 8(3) -- which determination governs on` `the day I am asking about` `when the new decision takes effect on` `the day the new decision takes effect`

§§ `9 Duration of assessed income period`

@export How long does my assessed income period last (s 9(1))?
GIVEN `the day the decision on my claim takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the decision on your claim take effect?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A `Length of an assessed income period`
DECIDE `how long my assessed income period lasts` IS
    `s 9(1) -- the length of the assessed income period for a decision taking effect on` `the day the decision on my claim takes effect` `for a claimant born on` `my date of birth`

@export Is my assessed income period still in force on a given day (s 9)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know where you stand? (Use today's date unless you are asking about another day.)
      `my sex` IS A Sex @desc Are you a woman or a man? (Section 1(6) treats them differently.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you reach, or did you reach, pensionable age (the age the Pensions Act 1995 sets for you)?
      `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, a woman born on your date of birth reach pensionable age? (If you are a woman, give the same day as the answer above.)
      `my partner and I are married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you married to, or in a civil partnership with, the person you live with? (No if you live alone or with someone you are not married to.)
      `my partner and I are members of the same household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and that person members of the same household?
      `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not married to or in a civil partnership with that person, do you live together as if you were?
      `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations say that, in your circumstances, you are not to be treated as living together as a couple?
      `my partner's sex` IS A Sex @desc Is your partner a woman or a man? (Answer anything if you have no partner.)
      `my partner's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your partner's date of birth? (Any date if you have no partner.)
      `the day my partner reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, your partner reach pensionable age? (Any date if you have no partner.)
      `the day a woman born on my partner's birthday reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day does, or did, a woman born on your partner's date of birth reach pensionable age? (If your partner is a woman, the same day as the answer above.)
      `the day my assessed income period began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your assessed income period begin (the day the decision took effect)?
      `I have become or ceased to be a member of a couple since then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since that day, have you become, or ceased to be, a member of a couple?
      `the first day on which I did` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day did that first happen? (Any date if not.)
      `the regulations under section 9(5) prescribe a further time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations under section 9(5) prescribe a further time at which your period ends?
      `that further time` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is that time? (Any date if not.)
      `the regulations stop the period ending at the events in section 9(4) in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations prescribe circumstances, in your case, in which your period does NOT end at the events in section 9(4)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `whether my assessed income period is in force on the day` IF
    `s 9 -- the assessed income period is in force on` `the day I am asking about` `my case` `my assessed income period`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day I reach pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my birthday reaches pensionable age`
        `my partner` MEANS Person WITH
            sex IS `my partner's sex`
            `date of birth` IS `my partner's date of birth`
            `day pensionable age is attained` IS `the day my partner reaches pensionable age`
            `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS `the day a woman born on my partner's birthday reaches pensionable age`
        `my household` MEANS Household WITH
            `married to or civil partners of each other` IS `my partner and I are married or civil partners`
            `members of the same household` IS `my partner and I are members of the same household`
            `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners`
            `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb`
        -- Placeholder: this question does not read this income.
        `my income` MEANS Income WITH
            earnings IS 0
            `working tax credit` IS 0
            `retirement pension income` IS 0
            `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS 0
            `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS 0
            `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS 0
            `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
            `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
            `income from capital` IS 0
            `income of a prescribed description` IS 0
        -- Placeholder: this question does not read this income.
        `my partner's income` MEANS Income WITH
            earnings IS 0
            `working tax credit` IS 0
            `retirement pension income` IS 0
            `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS 0
            `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS 0
            `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS 0
            `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
            `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
            `income from capital` IS 0
            `income of a prescribed description` IS 0
        `my case` MEANS Case WITH
            `day tested` IS `the day I am asking about`
            claimant IS `me`
            `other member of the couple` IS `my partner`
            household IS `my household`
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `in Great Britain` IS TRUE
