            `other member of the couple` IS `my partner`
            household IS `my household`
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `in Great Britain` IS TRUE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `temporarily absent from Great Britain and entitlement continued by regulations` IS FALSE
            `income of the claimant` IS `my income`
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `qualifying income of the claimant` IS 0
            `income of the other member` IS `my partner's income`
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `qualifying income of the other member` IS 0
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `severely disabled` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `claimant entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `other member entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `other member entitled to state pension credit` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `regulations under section 3ZA(1) prescribe the claimant's case` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `regulations under section 3(8) take the maximum savings credit to be nil` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `excluded by section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 as amended by section 4(2)` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `prescribed circumstances in which an amount below the prescribed amount is payable` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `a claim has been made and the Administration Act section 1 conditions are met` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `entitlement restricted by section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `either party to the marriage has a spouse additional to the other party` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `person, other party and additional spouse members of the same household` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: this question does not read this field.
            `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies` IS FALSE
        `my assessed income period` MEANS `Assessed income period` WITH
            `day the relevant decision takes effect` IS `the day my assessed income period began`
            `first day after that day on which the claimant becomes or ceases to be a member of a couple` IS IF `I have become or ceased to be a member of a couple since then` THEN JUST `the first day on which I did` ELSE NOTHING
            `first further time prescribed under section 9(5)` IS IF `the regulations under section 9(5) prescribe a further time` THEN JUST `that further time` ELSE NOTHING
            `prescribed circumstances in which the period does not end under section 9(4)` IS `the regulations stop the period ending at the events in section 9(4) in my case`

§§ `10 Effect of variations under section 7(4)`

@export What state pension credit am I paid on a given day once my income element changes (s 10(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know where you stand? (Use today's date unless you are asking about another day.)
      `the day my pension, or another item, changes` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the alteration come into force for you (the commencing date)?
      `an assessed income period is in force for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an assessed income period in force for you?
      `one of my retirement provision elements is varied under section 7(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount of one of the elements of your retirement provision varied in accordance with regulations under section 7(4)?
      `the variation changes the amount of state pension credit due to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the variation affect the computation of the state pension credit due to you?
      `the amount I am paid before the change` IS A NUMBER @desc How much state pension credit are you paid before the change, a week?
      `the amount I am entitled to after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are you entitled to once the change takes effect, a week?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the state pension credit I am paid on the day` IS
    `s 10(2), (3) -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` `the day I am asking about` `given the commencing date` `the day my pension, or another item, changes` `with an assessed income period in force` `an assessed income period is in force for me` `and a variation of an element` `one of my retirement provision elements is varied under section 7(4)` `that affects the computation` `the variation changes the amount of state pension credit due to me` `from the amount before` `the amount I am paid before the change` `to the amount after` `the amount I am entitled to after the change`

@export Must the Secretary of State make a new decision before my changed amount is paid (s 10(2))?
GIVEN `an assessed income period is in force for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an assessed income period in force for you?
      `one of my retirement provision elements is varied under section 7(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount of one of the elements of your retirement provision varied in accordance with regulations under section 7(4)?
      `the variation changes the amount of state pension credit due to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the variation affect the computation of the state pension credit due to you?
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `whether a new decision is needed before the changed amount is paid` IS
    `s 10(2) -- whether a further decision of the Secretary of State is needed for the changed amount to be payable` `an assessed income period is in force for me` `one of my retirement provision elements is varied under section 7(4)` `the variation changes the amount of state pension credit due to me`

§§ `Schedule 1 (Administration) and Schedule 2 (Minor and consequential amendments)`

@export Can I be asked for evidence about likely future changes in my circumstances (Sch 1 para 3(3A))?
GIVEN `the evidence is about the likelihood of future changes in my circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence you are asked for about the likelihood of future changes in your circumstances?
      `it is needed to decide whether to specify an assessed income period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it needed to decide whether a period should be specified as an assessed income period?
      `it is needed to decide how long that period should be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it needed to decide how long the period should be?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `whether I can be asked for evidence about likely future changes` IF
    `Sch 1 para 3(3A) -- the information or evidence is within what the regulations may require for state pension credit` `the evidence is about the likelihood of future changes in my circumstances` `it is needed to decide whether to specify an assessed income period` `it is needed to decide how long that period should be`

@export Can I appeal against this decision about my assessed income period (Sch 1 para 12)?
GIVEN `the decision I want to appeal` IS A `Decision about state pension credit` @desc Which decision do you want to appeal?
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `whether I can appeal against the decision` IS
    `Sch 1 para 12 -- an appeal lies against` `the decision I want to appeal`

@export What am I paid for a period of less than a week (Sch 1 para 13)?
GIVEN `the number of days my entitlement lasts` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days are you entitled to state pension credit in the period you ask about?
      `the amount the regulations prescribe for a period of less than a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount do the regulations prescribe for a period of less than a week? (0 if they prescribe nil.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `what I am paid for a period of less than a week` IS
    `Sch 1 para 13 -- the amount payable for a period of` `the number of days my entitlement lasts` `days` `given the prescribed amount` `the amount the regulations prescribe for a period of less than a week`

@export Will the Secretary of State pay for my medical exemption from wearing a seat belt (Sch 2 para 26)?
GIVEN `my partner and I are married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you married to, or in a civil partnership with, the person you live with? (No if you live alone or with someone you are not married to.)
      `my partner and I are members of the same household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and that person members of the same household?
      `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not married to or in a civil partnership with that person, do you live together as if you were?
      `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations say that, in your circumstances, you are not to be treated as living together as a couple?
      `I am in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in receipt of guarantee state pension credit?
      `my partner is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner in receipt of guarantee state pension credit? (No if you have no partner.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `whether the Secretary of State pays for my seat-belt exemption` IF
    `Sch 2 para 26 -- the Secretary of State makes the payment under section 70(2) of the Transport Act 1982 for` `my household` `I am in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` `my partner is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit`
    WHERE
        `my household` MEANS Household WITH
            `married to or civil partners of each other` IS `my partner and I are married or civil partners`
            `members of the same household` IS `my partner and I are members of the same household`
            `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners`
            `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb`

@export Am I free of a charge for a day-care service for a child in need (Sch 2 para 30)?
GIVEN `my partner and I are married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you married to, or in a civil partnership with, the person you live with? (No if you live alone or with someone you are not married to.)
      `my partner and I are members of the same household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and that person members of the same household?
      `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not married to or in a civil partnership with that person, do you live together as if you were?
      `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations say that, in your circumstances, you are not to be treated as living together as a couple?
      `I am in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in receipt of guarantee state pension credit?
      `my partner is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner in receipt of guarantee state pension credit? (No if you have no partner.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `whether I am free of the day-care charge` IF
    `Sch 2 para 30 -- the person is not liable to pay a charge under section 29(1) of the Children Act 1989 for a service under section 18(2) or (6) when` `my household` `I am in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` `my partner is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit`
    WHERE
        `my household` MEANS Household WITH
            `married to or civil partners of each other` IS `my partner and I are married or civil partners`
            `members of the same household` IS `my partner and I are members of the same household`
            `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS `my partner and I live together as if married or civil partners`
            `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS `the regulations take my partner and me outside the unmarried-couple limb`
